{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>I was sought.</b> This is the answer of HaShem: your fathers provoked me, yet I was sought. The meaning: I presented myself in distress, to a people that did not ask, that I might be found by them." "<b>I said, Here I am, here I am.</b> Time after time through the prophets." "<b>who did not call.</b> He was not called by my name in those days, but only by the name of Baal."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:58.106548862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}